 "title": "GIS / Mapping | Benton County, MN",
 "text": "GIS / Mapping | Benton County, MN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\n-->\nHow Do I...\nServices\nCommunity\nGovernment\nSearch\nCounty Surveyor\nInteractive GIS Mapping\nPlanning & Zoning\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nGIS / Mapping\nGIS / Mapping\nTo view property information please visit our Beacon site.\nOpen Data\nBenton County provides several GIS (Geographic Information System) datasets for the public to use. These files are shared in a zipped folder and include shapefiles and information about the data (called metadata).\nWe also have a map service that is updated every week and can be viewed on ArcGIS Online.\nBefore using the data, please read our disclaimer.\nYou can download 2023 aerial imagery from Benton County's ArcGIS Online page .\nDownload GIS Data\nAddress Points (ZIP)\nMinor Civil Divisions (MCD) (ZIP)\nParcels (ZIP)\nParks (ZIP)\nRoad Centerlines (ZIP)\nZoning (ZIP)\nCounty Maps\nBenton County Map (PDF)\nCommissioner Districts (PDF)\nCounty Facilities Map (PDF)\nPark Maps\nCounty Park Locations (PDF)\nBend in the River (PDF)\nMayhew Lake Park (PDF)\nSt. Regis Park (PDF)\nRose Anna Park (PDF)\nBenton Beach (PDF)\nOwnership/Plat Book Maps\nParcels 10 acres and greater (based on GIS acreage) are labeled. Labeled acreage shown is based off the deeded acres within the tax system. Ownership information is current as of the date shown in the bottom left corner of each page with annual updates planned.\nGeoreferenced PDF Maps\nAll ownership, plat book, and park maps on this page are georeferenced. This means they have location data built in, so you can see your current location on the map using a device with GPS.\nYou can use a smartphone, tablet, or other device with location services to view your location on the map—even without cell service.\nThere are several apps that work with these maps, including free ones like Avenza Maps . Just download the app and the PDF map to your device, and you’ll be able to use it offline.\nTownships\nAlberta (PDF)\nGilmanton (PDF)\nGlendorado (PDF)\nGraham (PDF)\nGranite Ledge (PDF)\nLangola East (PDF)\nLangola West (PDF)\nMayhew Lake (PDF)\nMaywood (PDF)\nMinden (PDF)\nSauk Rapids Twp (PDF)\nSt. George (PDF)\nWatab (PDF)\nCities\nFoley (PDF)\nGilman (PDF)\nRice (PDF)\nRoyalton (PDF)\nSartell (PDF)\nSauk Rapids (PDF)\nSt. Cloud (PDF)\nDisclaimer\nGIS data are maintained by Benton County for their intended use by Benton County and may be inaccurate for other use, and any person or entity seeking GIS data from Benton County expressly assumes that risk.\nNo warranties, expressed or implied are provided for the data herein, their use or interpretation. There are no warranties for the merchantability or fitness of the data for a particular purpose. Pursuant to Minnesota Statutes §466.03, subd. 21, Benton County does not guarantee the accuracy of the material herein contained and is not responsible for any misuse or misrepresentation of the information.\nContact Us\nScott Zwick\nGIS Coordinator\nEmail Scott Zwick\nPhone: 320-968-5075\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n531 Dewey Street\nFoley , MN 56329\n531 Dewey Street Foley MN 56329\nDirections\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 129\nFoley , MN 56329\nDirectory\n-->\nCareers\nPayments\nMaps\nContact Us\nAgendas & Minutes\nNotify Me\nContact Us\nBenton County Government Center\n531 Dewey Street\nP.O. Box 129\nFoley, MN 56329\nPhone: 320-968-5000\nQuick Links\nPay Your Property Taxes Online\nGovernment Center Project (Live Cam)\nWatch a County Board Meeting\nAgendas and Minutes\nWho's My Commissioner?\nCounty Parks\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nSite Map\nSalary Compliance Notice\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\nHome\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
